As an Android Kotlin developer in TourTrip.app:

## Core Standards
- **UI**: Jetpack Compose + Material 3; dynamic color theming; MotionLayout/Compose animations for 60fps.
- **Architecture**: MVVM + Repository pattern; Hilt DI; Room + DataStore; coroutines + Flow for reactive programming.
- **KMM Integration**: Use shared business logic from commonMain; keep platform-specific UI and system integrations in androidMain.
- **Networking**: Ktor client (shared) or Retrofit; OkHttp interceptors; timeout/retry/circuit breaker; TLS pinning for production.

## TourTrip.app Specifics
- **Offline-First**: Critical for travel scenarios; SQLDelight sync with server; offline maps caching.
- **Location Services**: FusedLocationProvider; background location with proper user consent; geofencing for tour alerts.
- **Maps Integration**: Google Maps/Mapbox; offline tile caching; route optimization; POI markers.
- **Payment Integration**: Google Pay; biometric authentication; secure card tokenization.
- **Push Notifications**: Firebase Cloud Messaging; travel updates; booking confirmations; emergency alerts.

## Security & Privacy
- **Data Protection**: EncryptedSharedPreferences for tokens; Android Keystore for payment data; no PII in logs.
- **Network Security**: Certificate pinning; network security config; API key obfuscation.
- **Permissions**: Runtime permissions with clear user-facing explanations; location accuracy options.
- **Authentication**: Biometric prompt API; session management; automatic logout on sensitive screens.

## Performance & Quality
- **Strict Mode**: Enable in debug builds; monitor main thread violations; database/network on background threads.
- **Memory**: Use Leak Canary; optimize image loading with Coil; lazy loading for large lists.
- **Background Work**: WorkManager for sync; foreground services for active trips; respect battery optimization.
- **Testing**: JUnit + MockK + Turbine for coroutines; Compose UI tests; baseline profiles for startup optimization.

## Build & CI/CD
- **Gradle**: Kotlin DSL; version catalogs; build types (debug/release/staging); signing configs external.
- **Code Quality**: ktlint + detekt; SonarQube analysis; dependency vulnerability scanning.
- **Release**: Automated builds; Play Console integration; gradual rollout strategy.

## Self-Check Protocol (Android)
Before submitting code:
- [ ] Compose previews render correctly across themes (light/dark/dynamic)
- [ ] No blocking operations on main thread (StrictMode validation)
- [ ] Hilt dependency graph validates without circular dependencies
- [ ] Room database migrations tested with instrumented tests
- [ ] Permissions requested with user-friendly rationale
- [ ] Offline functionality tested in airplane mode
- [ ] Memory leaks checked with LeakCanary
- [ ] APK size within budget (<50MB for main app)

## Soft Blocks (Android)
REJECT these patterns and suggest alternatives:
- ❌ Requesting location/camera permissions without clear user benefit explanation
- ❌ Storing payment tokens in SharedPreferences (use Keystore instead)
- ❌ Hardcoding API endpoints or keys in code (use BuildConfig or remote config)
- ❌ Creating fragments for new features (prefer Compose-first approach)
- ❌ Using deprecated APIs without migration plan
- ❌ Background location without foreground service and notification

## Error Handling Patterns
```kotlin
// Preferred: Sealed classes for result states
sealed class TourResult {
    data class Success(val tours: List<Tour>) : TourResult()
    data class Error(val exception: TourException) : TourResult()
    object Loading : TourResult()
}

// Required: Structured logging
Log.d("TourRepository", "Fetching tours", mapOf(
    "userId" to userId.masked(),
    "location" to location.toString(),
    "requestId" to requestId
))
```

## Dependencies Management
- Use version catalogs for consistency across modules
- Prefer Jetpack libraries over third-party when available
- Keep KMM dependencies in commonMain; Android-specific in androidMain
- Regular dependency updates with automated security scanning